course: dictionary
lesson: 4670
title: Holdfast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have an everyday meaning and a special meaning in one subject. «Seaweeds are algae with no roots, only a holdfast gripping the rock.» Here a holdfast is the part at the bottom of seaweed that holds it tightly to rocks.
explain: The sentence gives you clues. It says seaweed has no roots, so the holdfast is not a real root, even though it looks like one. Its job is to grip, not to take in food.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «only a grip gripping the rock» still makes sense. A holdfast can also be a clamp that holds wood to a workbench, so always look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: A holdfast is the root-like part at the bottom of seaweed.
fact: A seaweed's holdfast is not a real root: it grips the rock but does not take in food.
fact: «Bladder wrack» is a seaweed with air bubbles that lift it towards the light when the tide is in.
fact: In woodwork, a holdfast is a clamp or hook that holds wood firmly to the bench.
fact: You may meet the phrases «a kelp holdfast» and «a seaweed's holdfast» in science lessons on the seashore.
exercise: What is a holdfast in seaweed? | *The root-like part that grips the rock | The air bubble that floats the seaweed up | A fish that lives among the kelp
exercise: «Seaweeds are algae with no roots, only a holdfast gripping the rock.» What does this tell you about a holdfast? | It is a real root that drinks water | It is a kind of fish | It is a type of wood | *It grips the rock and does not take in food
exercise: In woodwork, what is a holdfast used for? | *Holding wood firmly to the workbench | Floating on the sea | Cooking a meal | Growing new leaves
test: Why is a seaweed's holdfast not really a root? | Because it floats on the tide | *Because it only grips the rock and does not take in food | Because it grows in the air | Because it is made of wood
test: Which phrase uses holdfast in the way the lessons show? | a holdfast fish | a seaweed bubble | a kelp root | *a kelp holdfast
exam: «The bladder wrack's air bubbles lift it towards the light when the tide is in.» What keeps the seaweed fixed in place? | *Its holdfast | The air bubbles | The sun | The tide
